" The Men Tsee Khang Institute for Astro and Medicine in Lhasa, TAR, is the central authority for traditional Tibetan medicine and astrology, two fields of research which are closely related in Tibetan tradition. The institute is in charge of editing the annual Tibetan calendar. Although this can be described algorithmically, in 2009 Men Tsee Khang experts have re-erected a calendar observatory in Stag Phu monastery, where a sunrise observation is performed on each March 17th for calibrating the calendar. On this day, just as the sun climbs over a mountain ridge, its first rays are cast through a window in the observatory tower onto a particular rock which has been embedded into a circular platform.\n"
"\n"
